 If an upstream behavior changes such that one of these additive features starts
 *conflicting* with upstream, promote it to `docs/parity/DIVERGENCES.md` with a numbered D
 entry and a SCRUTINIZED tag.
+
+## Native OAuth account support (bundled-host patch)
+
+The bundled host stores native OAuth accounts in `<agentDir>/oauth-accounts.json`.
+The store uses version 1, owner-only permissions, atomic replacement, and the existing bounded file-lock protocol.
+It limits each store to 256 accounts and 4 MiB.
+
+The host imports singleton OAuth credentials from `auth.json` on first account access.
+Migration preserves `auth.json` and records completed imports.
+API keys continue to use `auth.json`.
+Malformed account stores cause an error. The host does not replace their bytes.
+The legacy credential API still accepts partial OAuth values.
+These values remain in `auth.json`. Native login and account records require an access token.
+
+1. Use `/login openai-codex` to add a native Codex account.
+2. Repeat the login to add another account.
+3. Use `/accounts` to select an account.
+4. Use `/accounts list` to show safe labels and opaque IDs.
+5. Use `/accounts <id>` to select a known ID directly.
+6. Use `/logout` to remove only the selected account for a provider.
+
+Login selects its returned account identity.
+Repeated login updates the same identity without deleting other accounts.
+Selection persists per provider. Logout does not select another account.
+Request-time refresh updates only the selected account under both the account lock and the legacy lock.
+Both locks cover callbacks and durable native writes. Cancellation before admission does not run a callback or clear runtime credentials.
+Refresh rejects different identity claims only when both tokens contain the same claim.
+Missing claims and provider metadata changes do not change the opaque account ID.
+The built-in `openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol` model retains its native Codex backend.
+The separate `openai` API-audience login remains unchanged.
+
+Go extensions use `Context.OAuthAccounts()`, `Context.OAuthAccountAuth(id)`, and `Context.SelectOAuthAccount(id)`.
+RPC and TUI extensions use the same host bridge and request credential store.
+Enumeration does not refresh credentials.
+`OAuthAccountAuth` returns `type`, `access`, `expires`, and `accountId`.
+Never log, display, or persist this credential result.
 
